   "Wiki": "https://www.gem.wiki/Clifton_Pier_LNG_Terminal",
   "TerminalName": "Clifton Pier LNG Terminal",
   "UnitName": "--",
   "FacilityType": "import",
   "FacilityType [ref]": "https://www.compressortech2.com/news/shell-approves-bahamas-lng-regasification-terminal/8126907.article",
   "Fuel": "LNG",
   "Status": "construction",
   "Substatus": "actual",
   "Status [ref]": "https://www.turner-industries.com/projects/turner-industries-bahamas-services-new-power-for-new-providence/, https://www.bahamaslocal.com/newsitem/348112/PM_Davis_LNG_Terminal_groundbreaking_represents_his_Governments_commitment_to_build_an_energy_future_that_is_stronger_cleaner_and_more_reliable_for_our_people.html, https://www.datocms-assets.com/146580/1783403747-igu-world-lng-report-2026.pdf",
   "Country/Area": "Bahamas",
   "Researcher": "Gregor Clark",
   "LastUpdated": "2026-08-06",
   "ResearcherNotesUnit": "GC, Aug 2026: Shell took FID on this project in July 2026, and construction appears to have begun around the same time; first gas expected in Q1 2027. \"The terminal is designed to support baseload generation at Clifton Pier in excess of 170 megawatts, according to a Shell spokesperson.\"\nAL2025: Proposal has been revived by new government, with changes in ownership/operator. \nGC, Sep 2024: Shell appears to have definitively abandoned the Clifton Pier project in favor of a new LNG-fueled power plant at Blue Hills that will apparently not require a regasification facility. Gregor, July 2023: Capacity, cost, start year, and ownership percentages not available. This project has been on-again, off-again for years and appears to be indefinitely stalled, but still seems worth documenting in case it ever moves forward.",
   "ResearcherNotesProject": "GC, Aug 2026: Shell took FID on this project in July 2026; first gas expected in Q1 2027.\n\nAL2025: From what I've seen, the new deal is still unclear. I didn't add any phases because info is murky, but it might be built in anywhere between 1 and 4 phases. I'm also not sure whether the LNG terminal will still be located near Clifton Pier Power station, or whether it will be a floating/offshore terminal: “With respect to the purchaser of the fuel itself, it will be a government-owned special purpose vehicle (SPV) that will be responsible for purchasing the fuel from Shell and then reselling it to the different power generators.\" Initial project was agreement between BPL and Shell, but after being shelved, project was revived through a joint venture with FOCOL to build the terminal with Shell, and a PPA with Shell for the supply of LNG: \"The agreement for the development of the terminal and other facilities is a partnership between FOCOL Ltd. and Shell, while the LNG supply is an agreement with Shell alone.\"  See history details: https://www.thenassauguardian.com/business/govt-finalizes-lng-deal-with-shell-north-america-focol/article_5d1a429a-071c-44ff-9367-e39cfe6fdcdc.html",
